    "result_text": "All tests pass: **255 tests, 0 failures, BUILD SUCCESS**. (The stack-trace lines in the output are logged expected exceptions from a test that itself passed \u2014 its set reports 0 failures.)\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the disposable-email-domain blocklist for owner creation and updates.\n\n**New function** \u2014 `RejectDisposableEmailDomain.java`: reads the `@Val Owner`, extracts the domain after the last `@`, and throws the existing checked `InvalidEmailException` (which already maps to a 400 via `InvalidEmailExceptionHandler`) when the domain is one of `mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`. Absent/emailless owners pass through untouched.\n\n**Wiring** \u2014 added a `rejectDisposableEmailDomain` step to both endpoint pipelines, placed immediately after `normalizeEmail` so the check runs on the already-validated, lower-cased address (and before the write/save):\n- `owners.POST.yml` (`normalizeEmail \u2192 rejectDisposableEmailDomain \u2192 normalizeAddress`)\n- `owners/{ownerId}.PUT.yml` (`normalizeEmail \u2192 rejectDisposableEmailDomain \u2192 save`)\n\nThis follows the project's OfficeFloor conventions (one public method per step, `govern: [ transaction ]`, checked exception + escalation handler, reusing the existing `InvalidEmailException` rather than adding a new one). The new `AcceptanceTest.errorRejectsDisposableDomain` passes, and no existing tests regressed.",
